# Grouped Scatter Plot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Set `layout.scattermode: "group"` to display multiple scatter traces
side-by-side at each categorical x-axis position, similar to grouped bar
charts. Each trace needs the same x categories.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

categories = ["Category 1", "Category 2", "Category 3", "Category 4"]

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: categories,
    y: [4, 3, 5, 2],
    mode: "markers",
    name: "Group A",
    marker: %{size: 12}
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: categories,
    y: [3, 5, 2, 4],
    mode: "markers",
    name: "Group B",
    marker: %{size: 12}
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: categories,
    y: [5, 2, 4, 3],
    mode: "markers",
    name: "Group C",
    marker: %{size: 12}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(
  title: "Grouped Scatter Plot",
  scattermode: "group"
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
